# Contact-form email delivery, via Resend (https://resend.com).
#
# The site builds and every page renders without these values. Only the contact
# form needs them: without RESEND_API_KEY the form returns a 503 and tells the
# visitor to email directly, which is the honest failure rather than a silent one.
#
# Copy to .env.local for development. On Vercel, set these under
# Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables, then REDEPLOY: an existing
# deployment does not pick up a new variable on its own.
#
# Full setup, including the four DNS records, is in docs/contact-email.md.

# Required. Resend API key, created at https://resend.com/api-keys with
# "Sending access" only: the site never reads or lists email. Begins re_.
RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Required in production. The verified sender.
#
# This must be an address on a domain verified in the Resend account. A Gmail,
# Outlook or Yahoo address will NOT work here and the site refuses to send from
# one: nobody can verify ownership of those domains. Enquiries can still be
# delivered to such an address, which is CONTACT_TO_EMAIL below.
#
# Left unset, the site falls back to Resend's shared onboarding sender, which
# delivers only to the account owner. That is enough for a first smoke test, and
# it disables the visitor acknowledgement.
CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=Quiet Gears <enquiries@quietgears.co.uk>

# Optional. Where enquiries are delivered. Defaults to quietgearsai@gmail.com.
# Any mailbox works here, including Gmail.
CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=quietgearsai@gmail.com

# Optional. A second copy of each enquiry, for a shared archive.
# CONTACT_BCC_EMAIL=archive@quietgears.co.uk
